# ⛔⛔ THE BINARY'S NAME, AND IT WAS WRONG FOR AS LONG AS THE RENAME HAS BEEN
# DONE. These lines said /pkgm and /pkgm.*, which is what the command used to be
# called. After the rename to `zpkgm` nothing ignored the built binary any more,
# and a 14 MB arm64 Mach-O executable went into the repository and is in HEAD
# (blob e2ec8ed, 14 204 658 bytes). A rename is not finished when the code
# compiles: every file that names the old thing by spelling rather than by
# meaning stops working silently, and an ignore rule is the quietest of them.
/zpkgm
/zpkgm.*
*.out
bsd.test
bsd-tests.list
